// engram/internal/workflow/v1/workflow.proto
//
// Temporal payloads (workflow inputs, activity inputs/results). NEVER served over gRPC; encoded with the Temporal proto
// payload converter. Every input carries a WorkflowScope with (namespace_id, tenant_id, shard_id, epoch) so that
// workers never consult the catalog on the hot path (decision D4): the shard's `namespace_ownership` row verifies the
// epoch inside every activity transaction.
//
// Versioning: package version + `schema_version` on every top-level input. Adding fields is always safe (histories
// replay with defaults); removing or re-interpreting a field requires a `workflow.GetVersion` patch in the workflow
// code and a drain window for running histories (section 4.5).
//
// Pre-1.0 breaking changes are allowed (plan section 4.5). Every top-level input written by the D22 build carries
// `schema_version = 2`; the worker branches on it for in-flight histories started at 1 and keeps that branch until they
// have drained (30 days).
//
// Payload size and confidentiality (decision N59, review F-13/F-18/F-25):
//   * every activity result larger than 4 KiB travels by blob key under the
//     namespace prefix (extraction, embeddings, entity resolution, links); CommitChunkInput is keys-only, so a Temporal
//     history holds ids, hashes and keys — never fact text or vectors — and a document delete reaches it by deleting
//     the blobs;
//   * RetainDocument continues-as-new every 100 chunks or 20 MB of history;
//   * whatever still travels inline is encrypted at rest by a Temporal
//     DataConverter payload codec (AES-256-GCM). Decision N99 (review-2 G-20): the codec uses a PER-NAMESPACE data key
//     wrapped by the shard key (key id in the payload metadata, namespace id in the workflow header); deleting the
//     wrapped data key is the shredding step of a namespace or tenant delete, and a key version is destroyed only after
//     rotation time
//     + max workflow run timeout (7 d) + Temporal retention (7 d). The accurate statement is therefore: text appears in
//     histories only as ciphertext, at most 4 KiB per activity result, plus
//     ChunkWork.header/context/metadata_json/entity_hints; histories expire with retention 7 d and are unreadable after
//     key destruction.

